{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["Who joins a bond — the vocalization is with ḥet, like מִן הַחֶרֶב, תֹּאכַל הֶחָרֶב, and this proves וְחֹבֵר חֲבָרִים, from the pattern מֶלֶךְ — מְלָכִים, and like עֶבֶד — עֲבָדִים; so one says from חֶבֶר — חֲבָרִים. If the vowel of חָבֵר were with bet, like חָבֵר אָנֹכִי לְכָל אֲשֶׁר יְרָאוּךָ, יָרֵךְ גָּדֵר כָּתֵף וְגָזֵל, whose vowels are below, it should have said וְחֹבֵר חֲבֵרִים — like מִן יָרֵךְ — יְרֵכוֹ, גְּזֵלוֹ, חֲבֵרִים מַקְשִׁיבִים לְקוֹלֵךְ. And with ḥet, I afterward found in Sephardi codices according to this reading."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "Rashbam's phonetic argument involves letter names, vowel qualities, and construct-state forms; the technical terms 'vocalization is with ḥet/bet' (טעמו/ניגון בחי״ת/בבי״ת) refer to which consonant carries the syllable peak, which I render literally. The unaddressed Hebrew quotations are left as he cites them without addresses. The closing phrase כדברי likely means 'according to my reading/words.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:39:12.478309415Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}